                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Brad Bishop",
                        "email": "bradleyb@fuzziesquirrel.com",
                        "username": "bradbishop"
                    },
                    "message": "I've been wanting to see this class deprecated for a long time, so I'm glad to see this.  What motivated you out of curiousity?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
                    "line": 0,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Patrick Williams",
                        "email": "patrick@stwcx.xyz",
                        "username": "williamspatrick"
                    },
                    "message": "1. systemd.bbclass now does most of what we need out of the box, since it can actually set up template services now.\n2. systemd.bbclass and obmc-phosphor-systemd.bbclass collide in a specific case of a template service that expects to be started from multi-user.target.  obmc-phosphor-systemd needs the service named in SYSTEMD_SERVICE but systemd.bbclass triggers a systemd action that fails with the latest systemd."
                }
            ],
